      <h2>Data engineering is the center of my work.</h2>
      <p>
        My day-to-day technical world includes Databricks, PySpark, ETL, Azure, and Microsoft
        Fabric. I’m interested in the full path from raw data to a platform that people can
        trust and use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside that core work, I explore local AI and hardware performance. My current lab
        work uses llama.cpp on Windows to compare model sizes, quantization, context lengths,
        GPU offloading, throughput, and system resource use.
      </p>

      <h2>What guides the work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Understand the tradeoff, not just the recommended setting.</li>
        <li>Measure behavior on real hardware before drawing conclusions.</li>
        <li>Document the path so the result can be reproduced later.</li>
        <li>Prefer clear systems that are easier to operate and improve.</li>
      </ul>
